WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:03.770
-Hello, everyone, and welcome
back to the Captain's Quarters.

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:05.938
I have now been trapped inside
without an audience since March,

00:00:05.938 --> 00:00:07.439
and, as some of you have
noticed,

00:00:07.439 --> 00:00:08.874
that I've gone a little insane.

00:00:08.874 --> 00:00:10.810
Weird things have been happening
to my hair,

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:12.612
I befriended the wasps
in my attic,

00:00:12.612 --> 00:00:16.482
And for some reason I even went
on a lengthy and irrelevant rant

00:00:16.482 --> 00:00:19.585
about a 20-year-old TV show for
teens, "Dawson's Creek."

00:00:19.585 --> 00:00:21.487
-You know what they say, Seth.

00:00:21.487 --> 00:00:24.591
A creek is just a tiny ocean.

00:00:24.591 --> 00:00:27.126
-[ Chuckles ]
Who would say that and why?

00:00:27.126 --> 00:00:29.928
Oh, right, I've also become
friends with a talking painting,

00:00:29.928 --> 00:00:32.932
and by the way, I'm aware that
the Sea Captain character

00:00:32.932 --> 00:00:34.667
has been divisive.

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:38.138
Some of you love him.
Some of you hate him -- Dad!

00:00:38.138 --> 00:00:40.740
Some of you are just confused as
to why we've chosen to invest

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:42.609
so much of our time and energy
into this bit.

00:00:42.609 --> 00:00:44.611
So, we have decided to settle
this debate

00:00:44.611 --> 00:00:47.379
once and for all with a poll --
Should we keep the sea Captain?

00:00:47.379 --> 00:00:49.248
Yes or no.
To vote, just log on

00:00:49.248 --> 00:00:52.118
to www.google.com,

00:00:52.118 --> 00:00:54.353
type in Sea Captain,
but don't click search,

00:00:54.353 --> 00:00:55.855
take a screen shot,
print it out,

00:00:55.855 --> 00:00:57.623
write yes or no or it
with a Sharpie,

00:00:57.623 --> 00:01:00.826
and then mail it to wherever
your best guess is

00:01:00.826 --> 00:01:02.595
for the address I'm filming
the show at.

00:01:02.595 --> 00:01:05.030
We will reveal the poll results
at the end of the summer.

00:01:05.030 --> 00:01:08.868
-The only pole I'm interested
in is a fishing pole.

00:01:08.868 --> 00:01:10.770
-Jokes like that aren't
helping your chances

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:11.971
of sticking around, Sea Captain.

00:01:11.971 --> 00:01:13.573
-Okay.
-Speaking of psychosis,

00:01:13.573 --> 00:01:15.774
President Trump and his allies
in the right-wing media

00:01:15.774 --> 00:01:19.279
are once again amplifying
an unhinged viral video

00:01:19.279 --> 00:01:20.980
lying about the coronavirus.

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:23.616
For more on this,
it's time for A Closer Look.

00:01:27.387 --> 00:01:29.755
As the coronavirus pandemic
has spread out of control,

00:01:29.755 --> 00:01:31.490
so has misinformation about it.

00:01:31.490 --> 00:01:32.692
If you have Facebook,

00:01:32.692 --> 00:01:35.294
or an uncle who still wears
his class ring,

00:01:35.294 --> 00:01:36.729
you've probably heard
some of it.

00:01:36.729 --> 00:01:39.165
I'm pretty sure we've all gotten
at least one e-mail

00:01:39.165 --> 00:01:40.867
from a relative during this
whole thing

00:01:40.867 --> 00:01:42.469
with the subject line like...

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:49.976
...when we all know that
swallowing a candle

00:01:49.976 --> 00:01:51.444
and sticking garlic up your butt

00:01:51.444 --> 00:01:53.546
is number three on goop's
top 10 ways

00:01:53.546 --> 00:01:55.081
to relax on a job interview.

00:01:55.081 --> 00:01:57.349
And it won't shock you to learn
that a lot of the misinformation

00:01:57.349 --> 00:02:00.186
can be found on Facebook,
the Website you signed up for

00:02:00.186 --> 00:02:01.754
just to see
if your high school crush

00:02:01.754 --> 00:02:03.622
got married to that
son of bitch, Jeff.

00:02:03.622 --> 00:02:07.093
Well, A -- they did,
and B -- they also went crazy.

00:02:07.093 --> 00:02:09.395
A report in April collected some
of the most popular

00:02:09.395 --> 00:02:11.931
coronavirus myths circulating on
Facebook.

00:02:11.931 --> 00:02:13.366
Some examples include...

00:02:19.906 --> 00:02:21.908
There was a post claiming
you can hold your breath

00:02:21.908 --> 00:02:24.410
for 10 seconds to test yourself
for coronavirus

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:28.548
and another alleging that
someone named Dr. Mario Pesaresi

00:02:28.548 --> 00:02:30.250
had revealed that inhaling steam

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:32.852
is a natural remedy for
coronavirus.

00:02:32.852 --> 00:02:34.420
Well, if steam cures disease,

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:37.323
that would finally explain why
all New Yorkers on subways

00:02:37.323 --> 00:02:38.691
look so hale and hearty.

00:02:38.691 --> 00:02:41.694
The L train is more restorative
than an Icelandic spa.

00:02:41.694 --> 00:02:44.497
Second, I don't know
who Mario Pesaresi is,

00:02:44.497 --> 00:02:46.533
but he sounds like a doctor
Paulie Walnuts

00:02:46.533 --> 00:02:47.800
would be friends with on
"The Sopranos."

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:50.536
"What's that smell?"
"Oh, that's me, Ton.

00:02:50.536 --> 00:02:52.939
Dr. Pesaresi told me if I put
provolone in my pants,

00:02:52.939 --> 00:02:54.941
it would cure my you-know-what."
"I don't know what."

00:02:54.941 --> 00:02:56.975
"I got a genital discharge."

00:02:56.975 --> 00:02:59.746
"Ohh! We're eating here!"

00:02:59.746 --> 00:03:01.447
By the way, if you're offended,
you should know

00:03:01.447 --> 00:03:03.449
the writer who wrote that
is Italian-American.

00:03:03.449 --> 00:03:07.219
-Ah, Italy, the New Jersey
of Europe.

00:03:07.219 --> 00:03:08.688
-So is the writer who
wrote that.

00:03:08.688 --> 00:03:10.022
Mwah.

00:03:10.022 --> 00:03:12.191
Now, you've probably heard some
of the more infamous

00:03:12.191 --> 00:03:13.926
and ludicrous conspiracy
theories

00:03:13.926 --> 00:03:17.597
like the idea that 5G mobile
towers are spreading coronavirus

00:03:17.597 --> 00:03:19.231
or that it was created
by Bill Gates

00:03:19.231 --> 00:03:22.134
as a way to implant chips
into people through vaccines.

00:03:22.134 --> 00:03:25.338
Unfortunately, these ideas
aren't just confined

00:03:25.338 --> 00:03:26.572
to dark corners of the Internet.

00:03:26.572 --> 00:03:28.975
They often make their way into
the real world

00:03:28.975 --> 00:03:31.911
as we saw in April when
right-wing conspiracy theorist

00:03:31.911 --> 00:03:34.814
Alex Jones showed up to
an anti-lockdown protest

00:03:34.814 --> 00:03:37.249
in Texas.
You remember Alex Jones,

00:03:37.249 --> 00:03:38.851
the guy who always looks like

00:03:38.851 --> 00:03:40.953
he's trying to Hulk-out
but can't.

00:03:40.953 --> 00:03:45.558
I think because instead of gamma
rays, he was hit by ham-ma rays.

00:03:45.558 --> 00:03:47.560
-I like it.
-Jones led the crowd

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:50.095
in chants of
"Arrest Bill Gates."

00:03:50.095 --> 00:03:55.100
[ Crowd chanting
"Arrest Bill Gates!" ]

00:03:55.100 --> 00:03:57.870
The only police who should
arrest Bill Gates

00:03:57.870 --> 00:04:00.473
are the fashion police.
Bill, why can't you find a tie

00:04:00.473 --> 00:04:01.774
that goes down to your waist?

00:04:01.774 --> 00:04:03.609
You look like the assistant
manager at a GameStop.

00:04:03.609 --> 00:04:06.045
You and Trump need to split
the difference.

00:04:06.045 --> 00:04:07.312
You're an I.T. billionaire.

00:04:07.312 --> 00:04:09.148
Stop dressing like an I.T. guy.

00:04:09.148 --> 00:04:11.150
And then there are
the viral videos,

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:12.351
which might seem at first lance

00:04:12.351 --> 00:04:14.721
to come from reputable medical
professionals,

00:04:14.721 --> 00:04:17.323
repeating some of the wildest
debunked conspiracy theories

00:04:17.323 --> 00:04:19.559
about the origins or effects
of COVID-19.

00:04:19.559 --> 00:04:21.794
Like that infamous
"Plandemic" video,

00:04:21.794 --> 00:04:23.829
featuring Syosset Stevie Nicks,

00:04:23.829 --> 00:04:25.531
a person who claims,
among other things,

00:04:25.531 --> 00:04:28.868
that masks can somehow
"activate" coronavirus,

00:04:28.868 --> 00:04:30.336
that beaches
shouldn't be closed

00:04:30.336 --> 00:04:32.905
because they have restorative
properties that cure diseases,

00:04:32.905 --> 00:04:34.007
and that...

00:04:40.813 --> 00:04:42.281
Which is ridiculous for many
reasons.

00:04:42.281 --> 00:04:44.850
I mean, if the guy could create
a highly-infectious virus

00:04:44.850 --> 00:04:46.185
in a lab as part of
a secret plot

00:04:46.185 --> 00:04:47.487
to sell a money-making vaccine,

00:04:47.487 --> 00:04:49.255
don't you think
he could also learn

00:04:49.255 --> 00:04:50.556
how to throw a baseball?

00:04:50.556 --> 00:04:53.292
And then there were those two
Urgent Care doctors

00:04:53.292 --> 00:04:54.593
from Bakersfield, California,

00:04:54.593 --> 00:04:56.896
who falsely claimed
in a viral YouTube video

00:04:56.896 --> 00:04:58.864
that the virus just wasn't
as deadly

00:04:58.864 --> 00:05:00.432
as most other experts believed.

00:05:00.432 --> 00:05:02.634
They based that claim on some
extremely faulty data,

00:05:02.634 --> 00:05:06.472
which they arrived at through
some truly terrible math.

00:05:06.472 --> 00:05:08.808
Basically, they claimed that a
lot more people in California

00:05:08.808 --> 00:05:11.444
had been infected with the
coronavirus,

00:05:11.444 --> 00:05:13.612
which would make the percentage
of cases

00:05:13.612 --> 00:05:15.848
that result in death
a lot smaller.

00:05:15.848 --> 00:05:17.717
And they arrived at that
conclusion, in part,

00:05:17.717 --> 00:05:19.618
by taking the rate
of positive tests

00:05:19.618 --> 00:05:21.421
at the clinics they own

00:05:21.421 --> 00:05:22.989
and just extrapolating that rate

00:05:22.989 --> 00:05:24.556
to the entire California
population,

00:05:24.556 --> 00:05:25.991
which makes no sense.

00:05:25.991 --> 00:05:27.960
The people who walk into an
Urgent Care clinic

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:29.294
because they think
they might be sick

00:05:29.294 --> 00:05:31.730
aren't a representative sample
of the entire population.

00:05:31.730 --> 00:05:34.000
I mean, I know I've definitely
gone to Urgent Care

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:36.369
like four or five times to ask
them about a weird rash

00:05:36.369 --> 00:05:39.004
and been told it's just
New York skin.

00:05:39.004 --> 00:05:41.340
Could be bedbugs.
Could be a rat bite.

00:05:41.340 --> 00:05:43.375
Could be heat rash from having
your radiator

00:05:43.375 --> 00:05:44.677
stuck on high all winter.

00:05:44.677 --> 00:05:47.379
Could be irritation from a
cockroach in your kitchen

00:05:47.379 --> 00:05:48.614
smoking a cigarette.

00:05:48.614 --> 00:05:51.417
[ Inhales ] "I'm your new
roommate, and no,

00:05:51.417 --> 00:05:54.487
I won't wear a mask.

00:05:54.487 --> 00:05:56.555
We need to get organic soaps."

00:05:56.555 --> 00:05:58.357
As one biologist --
"I'm sorry.

00:05:58.357 --> 00:05:59.659
I draw the line at soaps.

00:05:59.659 --> 00:06:01.761
As one biologist who specializes

00:06:01.761 --> 00:06:04.063
in infectious disease modeling
put it,

00:06:04.063 --> 00:06:05.565
the doctors' method was...

00:06:10.336 --> 00:06:11.870
Which is ridiculous.

00:06:11.870 --> 00:06:13.639
You can't estimate the average
height of Americans

00:06:13.639 --> 00:06:15.307
from the players on an NBA
court.

00:06:15.307 --> 00:06:17.877
However, you can estimate the
average basketball skill level

00:06:17.877 --> 00:06:20.512
of Americans from the players
on the Knicks.

00:06:20.512 --> 00:06:22.615
In both of these cases, those
videos are not just seen

00:06:22.615 --> 00:06:24.316
by millions of people before
being taken down,

00:06:24.316 --> 00:06:26.652
they were also
amplified by right-wing media.

00:06:26.652 --> 00:06:29.755
The Sinclair Broadcast Group had
planned to air an interview

00:06:29.755 --> 00:06:31.691
with the star of "Plandemic"
this past weekend

00:06:31.691 --> 00:06:33.792
until it backed down
after an outcry.

00:06:33.792 --> 00:06:35.093
Although, even in their
statement

00:06:35.093 --> 00:06:37.063
withdrawing the segment,
they also seemed to defend

00:06:37.063 --> 00:06:38.798
their initial decision
a little, writing...

00:06:44.470 --> 00:06:46.139
That's not a justification
for saying

00:06:46.139 --> 00:06:48.140
whatever you want
without consequences.

00:06:48.140 --> 00:06:50.209
You guys love to talk about the
marketplace of ideas,

00:06:50.209 --> 00:06:54.180
but actual marketplaces are also
free to impose their own rules.

00:06:54.180 --> 00:06:56.282
Because if you just let everyone
and everything

00:06:56.282 --> 00:06:58.184
into the marketplace,
you get Etsy.

00:06:58.184 --> 00:07:01.687
"Happy birthday, Mark."
"Oh, a dream catcher...

00:07:01.687 --> 00:07:04.122
made of old... Fresca cans.

00:07:04.122 --> 00:07:05.891
You...shouldn't have."

00:07:05.891 --> 00:07:08.194
And I'm not saying free speech
should be regulated

00:07:08.194 --> 00:07:10.563
by the government,
but we can do things

00:07:10.563 --> 00:07:12.365
like, say,
break up big-tech companies

00:07:12.365 --> 00:07:13.999
so they don't have so
much monopoly power.

00:07:13.999 --> 00:07:15.834
Also, a marketplace of ideas,

00:07:15.834 --> 00:07:17.336
just like a marketplace
of goods,

00:07:17.336 --> 00:07:19.372
should be responsive
to criticism.

00:07:19.372 --> 00:07:22.107
In a real marketplace, you can't
just open a store

00:07:22.107 --> 00:07:23.509
called "Arsenic-fil-A"

00:07:23.509 --> 00:07:26.211
or "Toys R Us
and Us Toys R Knives."

00:07:26.211 --> 00:07:27.613
And then say, "You can't
criticize me.

00:07:27.613 --> 00:07:30.349
It's the free market."
Dangerous misinformation

00:07:30.349 --> 00:07:32.618
like this has been surging
during the pandemic,

00:07:32.618 --> 00:07:34.920
often with the help of prominent
figures on the right.

00:07:34.920 --> 00:07:37.289
The latest example
is a Facebook video

00:07:37.289 --> 00:07:39.858
staged and funded by a
right-wing dark money groups.

00:07:39.858 --> 00:07:42.595
The video, which was viewed by
over 20 million people

00:07:42.595 --> 00:07:45.531
before being taken down, claimed
you don't need to wear a mask

00:07:45.531 --> 00:07:48.467
because the anti-malaria drug
hydroxychloroquine

00:07:48.467 --> 00:07:50.569
is a cure for coronavirus,

00:07:50.569 --> 00:07:53.272
even though it's been repeatedly
disproven by study after study.

00:07:53.272 --> 00:07:55.708
Just last week, there was yet
another study

00:07:55.708 --> 00:07:57.476
published in the
New England Journal of Medicine

00:07:57.476 --> 00:07:59.378
which found that
hydroxychloroquine

00:07:59.378 --> 00:08:01.280
does not help COVID-19 patients.

00:08:01.280 --> 00:08:03.515
No drug has been studied this
much

00:08:03.515 --> 00:08:06.485
since those troublemakers
at Psi U conducted an experiment

00:08:06.485 --> 00:08:09.354
to see which strain of marijuana
makes DORITOS taste better.

00:08:09.354 --> 00:08:11.690
I hope you're happy, gentlemen,
You've all flunked out.

00:08:11.690 --> 00:08:15.027
And believe me, we all wish
hydroxychloroquine

00:08:15.027 --> 00:08:17.062
actually worked.
We wish everything worked.

00:08:17.062 --> 00:08:19.465
Everyone wishes there was a cure
for coronavirus.

00:08:19.465 --> 00:08:21.633
No one wants to be trapped
inside for this long.

00:08:21.633 --> 00:08:24.670
If hydroxychloroquine really
worked, I'd take an UberPool

00:08:24.670 --> 00:08:26.505
to Times Square to get coughed
on by a tourist

00:08:26.505 --> 00:08:27.573
just for old times' sake.

00:08:27.573 --> 00:08:30.109
Ah, Times Square...

00:08:30.109 --> 00:08:32.945
Where else in the world
can you get...

00:08:32.945 --> 00:08:34.046
M&amp;Ms?

00:08:34.046 --> 00:08:36.248
I can't wait to be first in line

00:08:36.248 --> 00:08:38.784
at my local bodega ordering
a bacon, egg, and cheese.

00:08:38.784 --> 00:08:40.620
Well, no, with my luck,
I'd be second in line

00:08:40.620 --> 00:08:41.787
behind a construction worker

00:08:41.787 --> 00:08:43.422
placing their order
for his entire crew.

00:08:43.422 --> 00:08:44.690
"[New York accent] On the fish
sandwich, I need

00:08:44.690 --> 00:08:48.160
pepper and a light hot sauce."

00:08:48.160 --> 00:08:49.862
[Normal voice]
I miss you, friend.

00:08:49.862 --> 00:08:52.030
I've cursed you under my breath,
but I do miss you now.

00:08:52.030 --> 00:08:55.401
But all the studies tell us
hydroxychloroquine doesn't work,

00:08:55.401 --> 00:08:56.936
and pushing it is dangerous,

00:08:56.936 --> 00:08:59.271
especially --
especially for people

00:08:59.271 --> 00:09:02.141
who actually need it for
conditions like lupus.

00:09:02.141 --> 00:09:04.476
After the President began
touting hydroxychloroquine

00:09:04.476 --> 00:09:06.045
for coronavirus
earlier this year,

00:09:06.045 --> 00:09:09.347
lupus patients struggled to get
it with one telling "USA Today"

00:09:09.347 --> 00:09:10.383
that because...

00:09:16.755 --> 00:09:19.058
That's horrible.
Lupus patients basically have to

00:09:19.058 --> 00:09:21.293
microdose a life-saving
medication the same way

00:09:21.293 --> 00:09:24.030
your recently-divorced aunt
microdoses LSD.

00:09:24.030 --> 00:09:25.564
"If I take the right amount,

00:09:25.564 --> 00:09:29.068
it's almost like Steve never
existed in this universe."

00:09:29.068 --> 00:09:31.937
And yet, because they've failed
on the pandemic response,

00:09:31.937 --> 00:09:34.439
and because they're desperate
for a magic fix

00:09:34.439 --> 00:09:35.808
that will make the
crisis go away,

00:09:35.808 --> 00:09:37.543
prominent figures on the right

00:09:37.543 --> 00:09:41.080
are now pushing the discredited
hydroxychloroquine video.

00:09:41.080 --> 00:09:43.816
The President's son, Don Jr.,
had his Twitter account

00:09:43.816 --> 00:09:46.185
partially locked for 12 hours
after tweeting the video

00:09:46.185 --> 00:09:47.720
to his 5 million followers.

00:09:47.720 --> 00:09:50.289
And then last night, he went on
Fox News to complain.

00:09:50.289 --> 00:09:51.924
-Now, Twitter takes me down
for that,

00:09:51.924 --> 00:09:57.095
but twitter has no
problem saying that coronavirus

00:09:57.095 --> 00:10:00.566
disinformation spread by the
Chinese government

00:10:00.566 --> 00:10:03.268
does not violate their rules.

00:10:03.268 --> 00:10:04.469
That's interesting.

00:10:04.469 --> 00:10:06.571
Jake Tapper himself

00:10:06.571 --> 00:10:09.975
a few weeks ago posted,
"Study finds hydroxychloroquine

00:10:09.975 --> 00:10:12.945
helped coronavirus patients
survive better."

00:10:12.945 --> 00:10:16.315
Now, why is Jake Tapper not
spreading misinformation

00:10:16.315 --> 00:10:18.117
but I somehow am?

00:10:18.117 --> 00:10:20.486
-It's fun when a dumb guy brings
printouts to an interview.

00:10:20.486 --> 00:10:22.721
It's like when the jock on
campus carries around a book

00:10:22.721 --> 00:10:24.456
to impress girls.
"Oh, this?

00:10:24.456 --> 00:10:26.826
Yeah, I was, uh, just reading
about my favorite author,

00:10:26.826 --> 00:10:28.928
Ernest Hemingway.
He went to jail.

00:10:28.928 --> 00:10:31.230
They, uh, made a movie
about it."

00:10:31.230 --> 00:10:32.631
Oh, wait, wait.
I'm sorry,

00:10:32.631 --> 00:10:35.934
what's on one of those
printouts?

00:10:35.934 --> 00:10:37.769
Oh, man.

00:10:37.769 --> 00:10:39.872
